praak.nl en de Mijn Rechtspraak-omgeving maken geen gebruik van PHP en zijn daarom gewoon beschikbaar.\nL21: ## Afzender\nL22: \nL23:   * 【3†Raad voor de rechtspraak】\nL24: \nL25: 【4†Deel dit nieuwsbericht via X - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†x.com】【5†Deel dit nieuwsbericht via Facebook - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.facebook.com】Deel dit nieuwsbericht via e-mail【6†Deel dit nieuwsbericht via LinkedIn - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.linkedin.com】\nL26:   * 【7†Volg ons op X (Twitter) - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†x.com】\nL27:   * 【8†Volg ons op Facebook - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.facebook.com】\nL28:   * 【9†Volg ons op Instagram - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.instagram.com】\nL29:   * 【10†Volg ons op Youtube - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.youtube.com】\nL30:   * 【11†Volg ons op LinkedIn - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†nl.linkedin.com】\nL31: \nL32:   * 【12†'Blijf op de hoogte' nieuwsbrief - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.nieuwsbriefrechtspraak.nl】\nL33:   * 【13†Sitemap】\nL34:   * 【14†Privacy】\nL35:   * 【15†Cookies】\nL36:   * 【16†Toegankelijkheid】\nL37:   * 【17†Spoofing】\nL38:   * 【18†Vacatures - U verlaat Rechtspraak.nl†www.werkenbijderechtspraak.nl】\nL39:   * 【19†Archief】\nL40:   * 【20†Over rechtspraak.nl】\nL41: \nL42:   * 【21†English】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHPの脆弱性対応に伴うJOGMECウェブサイトの再開について : お知らせ | 独立行政法人エネルギー・金属鉱物資源機構［JOGMEC］ (https://www.jogmec.go.jp/news/information/information_00710.html)\nciteturn92view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn90view0\",\"pattern\":\"2026年10月22\"}); Total lines: 912\nNo matching text found for \"2026年10月22\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCloudflare deploys protections against php2shell vulnerability | Cloudflare Blog (https://blog.cloudflare.com/php-vulnerabilities-waf-protection)\nciteturn92view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn90view2\",\"pattern\":\"2026-10-21\"}); Total lines: 1024\nNo matching text found for \"2026-10-21\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCloudflare deploys protections against php2shell vulnerability | Cloudflare Blog (https://blog.cloudflare.com/php-vulnerabilities-waf-protection)\nciteturn92view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn90view2\",\"pattern\":\"attack\"}); Total lines: 1024\nL862: ## New rules\nL863: \nL864: For Free customers, new rules have been released under the Cloudflare Managed Free Ruleset (Ruleset ID 77454fe2d30c4220b5701f6fdfb893ba). Free customers don’t have to take any actions to enable the protection. To override the ruleset behavior, you can refer to our 【820†documentation†developers.cloudflare.com】.\nL865: Rule Description   | Rule ID\nL866: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619)  | 4e315666e8e344cdb64119a3b5ccf32f\nL867: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #2  | 00c10e6cc4da4bd08722adeebcd95984\nL868: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #3  | 48ddf592361e4fdb97a8a85982dab691\nL869: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #4  | 3556683d512a47f2937899c524b1a4c6\nL870: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #5  | da07c85852e34625bb478496302ede46\nL871: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #6  | 19373a83abb840e18ab3ce5a7975ce1b\nL872: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #7  | 07f0b6ddaabf40b1b2042dade8d613fa\nL873: Protection for paid plans has been released as part of the Cloudflare Managed Ruleset (Ruleset ID efb7b8c949ac4650a09736fc376e9aee). If you are on a Professional, Business, or Enterprise plan, review your Managed Ruleset deployment to confirm it has 【821†deployed†developers.cloudflare.com】 block mode.\nL874: Rule Description   | Rule ID\nL875: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619)  | c1d409ad838f47f59446f21cc438d5dd\nL876: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #2  | f9a45927414245e3a64bb12d0a0c2f64\nL877: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #3  | 771c654ae1154d4daa72f4e1545d163c\nL878: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #4  | 217005865f0145f392300bac212afcc9\nL879: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #5  | 38efdb17ea594501bb55a1d71867b12e\nL880: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #6  | 4148ae686fdb4d01be673fab9d9c073d\nL881: PHP Remote Code Execution Attack (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619) #7  | 1389aa259617437392ce149c48143645\nL882: To better identify exploit attempts, Cloudflare developed full transaction detection, a new WAF capability that analyzes both sides of the same HTTP transaction. While some malicious payloads can be identified using the request alone, the response contains useful signals that can be used to create rules with higher confidence, reducing false positives. A matching full transaction rule can block the origin response before it reaches the requester.\nL883: Learn how it works in our full transaction detection 【822†blog post】.\nL884: The new Cloudflare Managed Response Firewall Default has been automatically deployed for customers on all plans, including Free. To verify that the response rules are active, you can visit the Security > Security Rules page. Read the full transaction 【822†blog】 to learn how to customize its deployment.\nL885: \nL886: 【823†Image: image5.png】\nL887: \nL888: The new Cloudflare Managed Response Firewall Default detection is protecting your traffic.\nL889: ## Review events and customize protection\nL890: \nL891: To analyze blocked requests, visit Security > Security Analytics > Events. Filter by the rule IDs in the table above and inspect the matched request, action, and path. Events identify whether the action came from a managed or custom rule. Customers who need to tailor the protection can 【824†update the scope†developers.cloudflare.com】 of the Managed Ruleset to the parts of an application where it is relevant.\nL892: ## Update PHP and keep the protection enabled\nL893: \nL894: Cloudflare customers using our Managed Ruleset are protected by default. We recommend following the 【814†advisory†www.php.net】 recommendation and applying the vendor update to your PHP repos as soon as possible while keeping the WAF protection enabled as an additional protection. Our WAF analysts will continue to update protections as new techniques emerge.\nL895: \nL896: Copy prompt to fix!Copy prompt to fix!Prompt copied!\nL897: \nL898: Discuss Online\nL914: ## Getting Started\nL915: \nL916:   * 【826†Plans†cloudflare.com】\nL917:   * 【827†Contact sales†cloudflare.com】\nL918:   * 【828†Partners†www.cloudflare.com】\nL919:   * 【829†Find a partner†partnerlocator.cloudflare.com】\nL920:   * 【830†Startups†www.cloudflare.com】\nL921:   * 【831†Under attack?†www.cloudflare.com】\nL922:   * 【832†Domain name search†domains.cloudflare.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHPの脆弱性対応に伴うJOGMECウェブサイトの再開について : お知らせ | 独立行政法人エネルギー・金属鉱物資源機構［JOGMEC］ (https://www.jogmec.go.jp/news/information/information_00710.html)\nciteturn92view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn90view0\",\"pattern\":\"13:20\"}); Total lines: 912\nNo matching text found for \"13:20\""
